# Backend structure (Tauri / Rust)

Organize Rust under `src-tauri/src/` by **layer**. Keep `main.rs` and `lib.rs` thin. Do not dump domain or I/O into `lib.rs`.

## Layout

```
src-tauri/src/
├── main.rs              # binary entry — only calls lib::run()
├── lib.rs               # Builder, plugins, generate_handler! only
├── error.rs             # AppError + Result alias
├── commands/            # #[tauri::command] — thin IPC boundary
│   ├── mod.rs
│   ├── workspace.rs
│   └── http.rs
├── domain/              # types + pure logic (no Tauri, no fs/network)
│   ├── mod.rs
│   ├── workspace.rs
│   └── request.rs
└── services/            # I/O and side effects
    ├── mod.rs
    ├── workspace_store.rs
    ├── fs_scan.rs
    └── http_client.rs
```

## Rules

1. **`main.rs`** only boots the lib. No commands, no business logic.
2. **`lib.rs`** wires the app: plugins, `invoke_handler`, state. No `fs` / HTTP / domain rules inline.
3. **`commands/`** = Tauri IPC only. Validate args, call `services/`, map errors. Keep handlers thin.
4. **`domain/`** = structs (`Serialize`/`Deserialize`), pure helpers. Must not depend on `tauri`, `AppHandle`, or do I/O.
5. **`services/`** = disk, network, `app.path()`, scanning dirs. May use `domain` types. No UI concerns.
6. **One module per domain** (`workspace`, `http`). Split into a folder when a file grows past ~200 lines.
7. **Do not create empty folders “for later”.** Add `http/` (etc.) when you need it.
8. Prefer a single `error.rs` (`thiserror`) over ad-hoc `String` errors everywhere; commands may still expose `Result<T, String>` at the edge if needed.

## Flow

```
Vue store → src/services/*.ts (invoke)
              ↓
         commands/<domain>.rs
              ↓
         services/<…>.rs  +  domain/<…>.rs
```

## Example — workspace directories

```
✅ GOOD
commands/workspace.rs       → load_workspace / add_directory
services/workspace_store.rs → read/write app_data_dir/workspace.json
domain/workspace.rs         → WorkspaceConfig { directories: Vec<String> }

❌ BAD
lib.rs                      → fs::write + serde_json + command body all inlined
commands/workspace.rs       → raw fs + path traversal with no service/domain split
domain/workspace.rs         → AppHandle / app.path()
```

## Alignment with frontend

| Rust | Frontend |
|------|----------|
| `commands/` | called via `src/services/` (`invoke`) |
| `domain/` | `src/types/` (keep JSON field names in sync) |
| `services/` | real I/O (frontend services only invoke) |

When adding a new backend capability (history, environments, send HTTP), add matching `commands/` + `domain/` + `services/` modules — do not append unrelated logic into an existing domain file or into `lib.rs`.
